👤 UserManager Utility
📌 Project Title

iUserManager Utility — Assignment 2

📝 Project Description

The iUserManager utility is a Bash Shell Script designed to simulate basic user and team management in Linux.

The utility allows us to create teams, add users under teams, manage user permissions, create shared directories, change user passwords and shells, and delete or list users and teams.

The project focuses on Linux users, groups, permissions, directories, and shell scripting.

🎯 Objective

The main objectives of this project are:

👥 Create and manage simulated teams.
👤 Create and manage users under a team.
🔐 Configure appropriate permissions for user home directories.
📁 Create shared team and ninja directories for every user.
🤝 Provide full access to members of the same team.
🥷 Provide full access to all ninjas through the ninja directory.
🔑 Change user passwords.
🐚 Change user shells.
🗑️ Delete users and teams.
📋 List users and teams.
🐚 Practice Linux user and permission management using Bash.
